  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-10T19:18:32.689Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The new bindings on the Oculus touch are just a really bad idea, in the beta i cant even turn around now while jumping because jump was on the joystick before, now its the A button, i would rather prefer bring up the menu with the A button rather than the joystick. Or please do make it possible to change the bindings for ourself, more since now i have no room left within the oculus touch buttons to use the playspace mover properly, X and A button was used for this by me and probably by most of the people. I would rather keep my X button for the playspace mover and the left joystick to reset the playspace and have the A button for the menu or if i could keep both X and the A button for playspace mover and have the 3.0 menu only on my right hand with the B button which would be great since i only ever use the VRChat menu on my left hand.\nThe other things is the fist hand gesture now needs both the Grips and Triggers held on the oculus which is really awkward, no idea why this changed.\nEven if the current binding stays i wont care if we get an option to customize the buttons for ourself.\nAnyway otherwise i like the entire idea of this update with the customizable menus just few fine tune is needed with the bindings.",
